<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If70fc40866e775f8903050628ff5a649dbbe421e" commit="a235d507e59941015dee1a520d603b137ecab285" commit_message="quipper: Put compat layer implementation-specific details in own dir.  Move implementation-specific content to compat/cros/detail. Other implementations can have a similar compat/&lt;your-impl&gt;/detail providing the necessary interfaces, and need only provide the correct compiler flags to have compat/&lt;your-impl&gt; found.  TEST=compiles BUG=none  Change-Id: If70fc40866e775f8903050628ff5a649dbbe421e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354204 Commit-Ready: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chong Jiang &lt;chongjiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="354204" owner_email="dhsharp@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/04/354204/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icad63de7ac009cc5e6a71c9238ffa8bab21dc006" commit="5a4b0bb39fb9ecaa0c9b521388033e4ef477f3b8" commit_message="quipper: Add compat/thread.h wrapper for a Thread class  TEST=none BUG=none  Change-Id: Icad63de7ac009cc5e6a71c9238ffa8bab21dc006 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354205 Commit-Ready: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chong Jiang &lt;chongjiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="354205" owner_email="dhsharp@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/05/354205/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I033fd0e187b2af155e826f0d0d872f25b1464072" commit="d0f338d995660166ab2f1c7135bb9c83575bb30c" commit_message="quipper: Add Notification class to compat layer threading  TEST=none BUG=none  Change-Id: I033fd0e187b2af155e826f0d0d872f25b1464072 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354206 Commit-Ready: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chong Jiang &lt;chongjiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="354206" owner_email="dhsharp@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/06/354206/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I815fb8d078ac30a08105c9bb3eacc1cedada320b" commit="069aa7dbfddd59d0f1e8cd02b26fae42596df450" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: handle channel survey wmi event 10.4 based firmware  Currently, channel survery events are not processed for 10.4 firmware based solutions. This patch will extend the support.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53741 TEST=Build, bring up wifi and basic sanity test.  Change-Id: I815fb8d078ac30a08105c9bb3eacc1cedada320b Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354296 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354296" owner_email="Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/96/354296/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3cc1ca597dbefa398998b87d23f3df4a38e9bb42" commit="d1a320881bd14128b0f1fab04395c14859860118" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: simplify pktlog htt event processing  It is expected that all pktlog events for 10.4 firmware based solutions should come through CE8 where as in case of 10.2 firmware based solutions, it should come through one of the HTT events (HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_PKTLOG).  But from experiments with 10.4 based solutions, it is observed that pktlog event for ATH_PKTLOG_TYPE_TX_MSDU_ID is coming through HTT pktlog event. Currently, we always parse with 10.2 pktlog header which will lead to pktlog decoding issues (payload length mismatch exceptions)  For trace points, it is required to provide only the payload size. So simplify the payload size calculation without the use of ath10k pktlog headers.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53772 TEST=Build, bring up wifi and basic sanity test.  Change-Id: I3cc1ca597dbefa398998b87d23f3df4a38e9bb42 Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354297 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354297" owner_email="Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/97/354297/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I040d3d648a284b9878eb1b793c8ccbfa726dfe96" commit="129295e0194d3c602e41e664f70b6b72767df61e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: hard code hw_rev enum value of QCA4019  Currently, wireless-4.2 stack in brillo doesn't have the latest ath10k source from upstream. In upstream, there are additional hardwares/chipsets supported by ath10k. With this addition, the hardware revision (hw_rev) enum value for QCA4019 is moved to 6 from 4.  Hardware revision (hw_rev) helps to determine the firmware variant sending these trace events.  It is important to have this hw_rev in sync with upstream thereby we can use the upstream tracing plugin to decode trace data.  So fixing the hw_rev of QCA4019 to 6. Added a note to remove this when we upgrade the wireless stack of 3.18  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53772 TEST=Build, bring up wifi and basic sanity test. Use uptramed tracing plugin and verified decoding of pktlog works  Change-Id: I040d3d648a284b9878eb1b793c8ccbfa726dfe96 Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/355372 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="355372" owner_email="Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/72/355372/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ide6973b59ee5281124853acfd69eda394166346c" commit="7ee7eb2ce9a852a0454a7597bfe321a6083c9daf" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ARM: dts: rockchip: add SPI flash node for rk3288-veyron  This is a standard binding for describing SPI flash that can be identified by reading their JEDEC ID. Let's use it.  Tested on Veyron Jaq.  Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;computersforpeace@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt; (cherry picked from git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/mmind/linux-rockchip.git for-next  commit 9a205e33d0dc81121d1a2417b33b55682b81b84d)  BUG=chromium:605253 TEST=boot on veyron_jaq; play with flashrom  Change-Id: Ide6973b59ee5281124853acfd69eda394166346c Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350880 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="350880" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/80/350880/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I93844cbf6fcb6c25b662dd277d90f2caeca5514c" commit="3231eab753d8a697d84c90d2a6bcfb9da62846c2" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: turn on MTD/M25P80 for armel  Veyron devices use SPI flash that can be supported by the MTD m25p80 driver.  These configs mostly match the arm64 selections:  CONFIG_MTD=y CONFIG_MTD_CMDLINE_PARTS=y CONFIG_MTD_M25P80=y CONFIG_MTD_OF_PARTS=y CONFIG_MTD_PARTITIONED_MASTER=y CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR=y CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR_USE_4K_SECTORS=y  and the rest are at defaults (=n).  BUG=chromium:605253 TEST=boot on veyron_jaq; play with flashrom  Change-Id: I93844cbf6fcb6c25b662dd277d90f2caeca5514c Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350881 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="350881" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/81/350881/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I276eab9f484c70aede004bee1a2eb5f4b71e7bbb" commit="e9508ed9c75de08c21b4dcffdde2856940d6d27d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: arm64: Provide &quot;model name&quot; in /proc/cpuinfo for PER_LINUX32 tasks  This patch brings the PER_LINUX32 /proc/cpuinfo format more in line with the 32-bit ARM one by providing an additional line:  model name      : ARMv8 Processor rev X (v8l)  Cc: &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; Acked-by: Will Deacon &lt;will.deacon@arm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Catalin Marinas &lt;catalin.marinas@arm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Will Deacon &lt;will.deacon@arm.com&gt; (cherry picked fr